# audit: `unwrap_or`, `is_ok`, `null`, `Box::new`, a `for` over an integer
# range's desugared `into_iter`/`next`, … are skipped on both sides) —
# foreign items, std callees, local bodies, upstream functions, indirect
# calls (`<indirect>`) — read from census_shapes.rs (NOT from the dump):
# I-EFFECTS-COVERED compares them with the trust-ir. Constructors (`Ok`,
# `Strip { .. }`) are not calls. The HIR site census is the site-kind
# subset of these rows plus the `site` rows (bodies the producer refused).
# The `drops` rows are typeck's facts: the locals, temporaries and by-value
# parameters whose drop glue may have a platform effect (an fd carrier, a
# Drop impl), read from the source; an empty row is "none".

